---
const items = [
  {
    q: "What exactly do I get when I buy?",
    a: "Two git repositories: launchkit-api (Django + DRF) and launchkit-web (Next.js 16 + React 19). Plus the AI-agent skills, the CLAUDE.md files, the CI configuration, the test suites, and a CHANGELOG. Everything that ships v1.0 — yours."
  },
  {
    q: "Can I use it for commercial projects? Multiple projects?",
    a: "Yes — both licenses include unlimited commercial projects, including client work. The only thing you can't do is resell the boilerplate itself as your own boilerplate product."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between Standard and Lifetime?",
    a: "Both ship the same source code, both let you build unlimited projects. Standard includes 1 year of updates and community support (Discord). Lifetime includes updates forever, priority email support, a 30-min onboarding call, and a private Slack channel — best if you plan to keep building SaaS for years."
  },
  {
    q: "Do I have to credit LaunchKit anywhere?",
    a: "No. Strip every reference to LaunchKit from the codebase. Rename every file. Use it however you want."
  },
  {
    q: "How do updates work?",
    a: "We push to a private GitHub repo you'll be invited to as a collaborator. Pulling updates is a normal git fetch + merge. Each release ships with a CHANGELOG and migration notes when relevant."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the refund policy?",
    a: "14 days, no questions asked. If the kit doesn't fit your project, email us and we'll refund the full amount. We'd rather you ship something you actually want to use."
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to know Django and Next.js to use this?",
    a: "Yes — this is a foundation, not a no-code product. If you've shipped anything in either framework, you'll be at home. The bundled CLAUDE.md files and skills make it easier to onboard with any AI coding assistant."
  },
  {
    q: "Is the multi-tenant model strict isolation or schema-per-tenant?",
    a: "Logical isolation: every tenant-scoped model carries a tenant FK and the middleware sets request.tenant. ViewSets auto-scope queries. This is the right tradeoff for early-stage SaaS — schema-per-tenant adds operational complexity that you don't need until you hit thousands of tenants."
  },
  {
    q: "What if I find a bug or need a feature?",
    a: "Standard gets community support via the buyers-only repo issues. Lifetime gets priority email support and a private Slack channel. Either way: we read every report, and security fixes are pushed to all license holders for free."
  }
]
---

<section id="faq" class="border-b border-border/60">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <span class="lk-section-num">09 / FAQ</span>
        <h2 class="lk-display lk-balance mt-4 text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
          The honest answers.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Anything else?
          <a
            href="mailto:hello@launchkit.dev"
            class="lk-link text-foreground"
          >Email us directly</a> — we read every message.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <ul class="flex flex-col">
          {
            items.map((item, i) => (
              <li class="border-t border-border/60 first:border-t-0">
                <details class="group/faq py-1">
                  <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-baseline gap-5 py-5 select-none">
                    <span class="lk-section-num shrink-0 group-open/faq:text-coral transition-colors">
                      {String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
                    </span>
                    <span class="lk-display flex-1 text-xl md:text-2xl leading-tight">
                      {item.q}
                    </span>
                    <span
                      aria-hidden="true"
                      class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground group-open/faq:rotate-45 group-open/faq:text-coral transition-transform duration-200"
                    >
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <path d="M8 3v10M3 8h10" stroke-linecap="round" />
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="pl-12 pr-2 pb-6 text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    {item.a}
                  </div>
                </details>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Remove default details marker — already replaced with our + → × icon */
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  details > summary {
    list-style: none;
  }
</style>
